      "description": "Despair is the collapse of hope — the inner state of the person who has stopped believing that things can be otherwise. The biblical vocabulary includes a Hebrew term that literally means not faithful, the failure of the capacity to trust, alongside images of devastation and the shattering of expectation. Despair is the most complete form of hopelessness: not just sadness but the extinction of the conviction that goodness is possible or that God is present. The psalms are unflinching in naming it.",
